guv(){return'1. Terms and Conditions of Use (T&C)\nLast Updated: February 06, 2026\n\n1.1 Agreement to Terms\nBy downloading, installing, or using PlanIt, you expressly acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agreed to be bound by these Terms and Conditions and our Privacy Policy. If you do not agree to these terms, you must not use the Application and must delete it immediately.\n\n1.2 Eligibility\nThe Service is intended for users who are at least 13 years of age (or 16 in certain jurisdictions). Minors represent that they have parental consent to use the App.\n\n1.3 Subscription and Payments (RevenueCat)\n- Payments are processed via Apple App Store or Google Play Store through RevenueCat.\n- Refund Policy: All transactions are subject to the refund policies of the respective Store. PlanIt does not issue direct refunds.\n\n1.4 Intellectual Property\n- PlanIt Content: All logos, designs, source code, and original content are the property of Stefano Di Masi (Dimadevs).\n- User Content: You retain ownership of your travel data. Images and screenshots remain exclusive to the user\'s private account.\n- Digitization Tools: OCR and AI tools are intended for private and personal use only.\n\n1.5 Limitation of Liability\n- "As Is" Basis: The App is provided without warranties. We do not guarantee the accuracy of data from third-party APIs.\n- Maximum Liability: Total liability is strictly limited to the amount paid for the subscription in the six (6) months prior to the claim. If no fee was paid, liability is zero.\n\n1.6 Governing Law\nThese terms are governed by the laws of Italy. Disputes shall be settled in the courts of Milan.\n\n1.7 Third-Party Services\nPlanIt uses affiliate links. We are not responsible for bookings or payments on third-party websites.\n\n1.8 User Conduct\nUsers are responsible for uploaded content and agree to indemnify Stefano Di Masi (Dimadevs) against claims resulting from misuse.'},
guc(){return'2. Global Privacy Policy\nLast Updated: February 06, 2026\n\nIntroduction\nYour privacy is a priority for PlanIt. By using the Application, you confirm that you have reviewed and understood how we protect your data.\n\n2.1 Information We Collect\n- Personal Data: Email address, Firebase UID.\n- Activity Data: Trip itineraries, dates, and locations.\n- Multimedia Access: Upon consent, the App may access the Photo Library or Camera. Images are private and stored securely on Firebase.\n- Technical Data: Device type, OS, and approximate location.\n\n2.2 Legal Basis\nProcessing is based on Contractual Necessity and Consent (for camera, gallery, and location access).\n\n2.3 Data Retention and Deletion\n- Account Deletion: The "Delete Account" feature permanently erases all personal data, images, and trip records from our servers.\n\n2.4 Third-Party Sharing\n- Google Gemini: Processes text to format trip details. No PII is intentionally transmitted.\n- RevenueCat: Used for subscription management.\n\n2.5 Security\nWe use Firebase Security Rules to ensure that your private data is accessible only by your authenticated account.\n\n2.7 Admin Access\nBackend access is restricted to authorized personnel via Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA).\n\n2.8 Affiliate Tracking\nThird-party affiliate networks may use cookies governed by their respective privacy policies.\n\n2.9 Contact Us\nFor privacy-related requests: dimadevs.staff@gmail.com'},
